    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Spring weather acted as a catalyst for movement, shaping a surge in the flow of people apprehended by a border security agency. Guardians of the boundary reported this increase, yet the overall immigration statistics tell a different story: year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows, a consequence of severe restriction. This tension between the data and the rigid system highlights builders of a new framework paralyzed by indecision, unable to craft a solution to the funding dispute.",
